window.docContents[7].resolve({"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L2-___-The-pair-is-a-system-too--Questions-to-ask-the-model-so-far":{"contents":"* Question* Check* What the verdict means\n* Where does total mass live?* pair_mass* On Composite.whole; the two body masses assemble there.\n* Can compressed and stretched configurations of pair P be compared by kC extension?* opened_pair* Yes; the typed displacement difference has magnitude stretched.extension .kC - compressed.extension .kC.\n* Can a whole mass be added to one of its parts?* refused_whole_part* No; their composite object indices differ.\n* Can two pairs' whole masses be added when their parameters are identical?* refused_whole_part* No; nominal PartOf .P and PartOf .Q have distinct bearer types independent of parameter values.\n* Does angular frequency assemble across the pair's bodies?* refused_frequency_assembly* No; the pair sort has no angular-frequency license.\n* What sort bears the normal mode?* normal_mode* The dedicated kind is attached to pairS, not bodyS or springS.\n* What happens to stiffness when kA and kC act in parallel?* parallel_stiffness, parallelLaw* The effective magnitude is their sum, and the measurement is extensive.\n* May the same summation rule be used for springs in series?* refused_series_stiffness, seriesLaw, licenseCashed* No; kA–kB reads 6 ∥ 3 = 2, and a hypothetical sum license reports 9. The Int examples are exact only for the exhibited pairs, not longer chains.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Onboarding: Human Context Protocols\u0009L2 — The pair is a system too","header":"5.3.9. Questions to ask the model so far","id":"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L2-___-The-pair-is-a-system-too--Questions-to-ask-the-model-so-far"},"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L2-___-The-pair-is-a-system-too--Synopsis":{"contents":"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Onboarding: Human Context Protocols\u0009L2 — The pair is a system too","header":"5.3.1. Synopsis","id":"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L2-___-The-pair-is-a-system-too--Synopsis"},"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--The-object-type--Assembly-over-a-composite--Two-sums___-and-only-the-object-tells-them-apart":{"contents":"A sum of quantities appears in applied models in two shapes that are identical on the page.\n\nA resultant combines several quantities of one object and one kind into one of the same\nobject and kind: the forces acting on a particle, the currents into a node. Nothing about the\nobject changes, so nothing beyond the scale gate addition already demands is needed.\n\nAn assembly combines the quantities of the parts into a quantity of the whole. The\nobject changes, and whether that is meaningful at all is a fact about the kind — which is what\nthe license records.\n\nSumming the particles' velocities is refused because it is an assembly of an unlicensed kind.\nSumming the forces on one particle must not be refused, because it is not an assembly. A layer\nthat indexes quantities only by kind writes both with the same ∑ at the same type and can\nrefuse neither; this is the clearest single thing the object index buys, and the\nPointParticle case study scores four designs on exactly it.\n\nThe license, cashed. For a kind that is genuinely extensive under a measurement, the assembled magnitude over any decomposition is the value that measurement reports for the whole. This is what makes the license a claim about the world rather than a permission slip: the class licenses the sum to be written, and this theorem is what shows the sum is right. Volume on mixing has no Extensive witness, so it has no instance of this.\n\nextensive_additive applied to the decomposition, symmetrized: the assembled magnitude is leafSum by definitional unfolding of the shared fold, and leafSum is the whole's measured numeral by the aggregation capstone.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009The object type\u0009Assembly over a composite","header":"16.5.1. Two sums, and only the object tells them apart","id":"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--The-object-type--Assembly-over-a-composite--Two-sums___-and-only-the-object-tells-them-apart"}});